pull -q; git log --oneline | head -3; git diff $OLD HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-1200 | head -30"]], "output": "```console\n0e7a30c Outline rev 8: Brief rev 7 thesis, P2 wording, P6 as C9\n73ca449 Outline rev 7: apply idea-review (C6 absolute R2 and wording, C1, C4, C5, Tier A)\n59cff62 Outline rev 6: results status per claim, thesis the results carry\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n-# Outline — what the paper says and what carries it (revision 6: first results from `analysis`, verdicts per claim)\n+# Outline — what the paper says and what carries it (revision 8: verdicts per claim; review #5 applied; Brief rev. 7 thesis and P6 added)\n-Source: `idea-repo` Brief revision 6 (the idea, the predictions P1–P5, the study design and cell budget), the objective (`story-repo`#1) and `prior_work.md`. This page says *what to test and where it shows*, never what a result must be. Every claim below has a \"refuted if\" line; a result that triggers it changes the claim, and I take it to `idea-repo` (see \"When results do not carry it\").\n+Source: `idea-repo` Brief revision 7 (the idea, the predictions P1–P5, the study design and cell budget), the objective (`story-repo`#1) and `prior_work.md`. This page says *what to test and where it shows*, never what a result must be. Every claim below has a \"refuted if\" line; a result that triggers it changes the claim, and I take it to `idea-repo` (see \"When results do not carry it\").\n-**C1 — Variance follows leverage (a reference, not the headline).** Var(τ̂) ≈ σ²L/n with L = Δxᵀ Σ̂⁻¹ Δx ≈ (1+d)/(p(1−p)); error grows with n⁻½, d^½ and the p(1−p) factor in noise-dominated cells. The *finding* is the departure: where σ²L/n over/under-states realised variance (hubs/BA, cluster designs, degree-correlated baselines, 2-hop features) and by what factor (effective n). *Evidence*: σ=0.25/0.5/1 slices, n slice (A2; without it no n-exponent exists), ER/SBM vs BA/WS, log-log fits of RMSE on n, d, p(1−p) with CIs (the d-exponent rests on three degrees {5,20,80}; reported as such with its CI); departure ratio realised/(σ²L/n). *Figure 2*: realised variance vs σ²L/n across cells, coloured by graph family (identity line), with the departure ratios. *Refuted/changed if*: iid-calibrated formula fails on the graphs where it should hold (ER/SBM, Bernoulli) → look for dependence among units; heavy tails → effective n.\n+**C1 — Variance follows leverage (a reference, not the headline).** Var(τ̂) ≈ σ²L/n with L = Δxᵀ Σ̂⁻¹ Δx ≈ (1+d)/(p(1−p)); error grows with n⁻½, d^½ and the p(1−p) factor in noise-dominated cells. The *finding* is the departure: where σ²L/n over/under-states realised variance (hubs/BA, cluster designs, degree-correlated baselines, 2-hop features) and by what factor (effective n). *Evidence*: σ=0.25/0.5/1 slices, n slice (A2; without it no n-exponent exists), ER/SBM vs BA/WS, log-log fits of RMSE on n, d, p(1−p) with CIs (the d-exponent rests on three degrees {5,20,80}; reported as such with its CI; the CIs are MC-only and treat the 42 cells as independent although they share graphs and draws, which the text says); the d-exponent is compared with the exponent of the *realised* L on the same cells, not with ½ (since (1+d)^½ is an approximation to L^½, the gap between 0.55 and ½ is partly a statement about that approximation); departure ratio realised/(σ²L/n). *Figure 2*: realised variance vs σ²L/n across cells, coloured by graph family (identity line), with the departure ratios. *Refuted/changed if*: iid-calibrated formula fails on the graphs \n-**C2 — Bias is set by curvature × corner distance, largely independent of d.** For a response curved in exposure, linear-fit spillover bias ≈ −½g''(1−2p) (+ third-order term); zero at p=½ to second order; for threshold responses with threshold outside the observed support the linear fit sees no spillover and the bias is the whole jump, independent of d in the limit of large d; at small d the support straddles the threshold and the bias is smaller or of opposite sign (`analysis` plan §3: the threshold slope does depend on d; the d-independence holds for smooth responses). Flexible lear\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "36666b8d-0414-57af-96cc-e5bb03998231", "at": 1795646217.333824, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 52019, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "57cf0aaec458f4f34212abe4a4140387", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "d9e21fe5-f9f2-589c-8f1a-34435bf2a622", "at": 1795646217.3415012, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 52020, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "57cf0aaec458f4f34212abe4a4140387", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "46969de3-d7db-5ad3-a58c-9c66b05cdba2", "at": 1795646217.345666, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 52021, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "57cf0aaec458f4f34212abe4a4140387", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "8ce8c733-a708-544d-b608-3bcf5952cbc5", "at": 1795646217.4256968, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 52023, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "57cf0aaec458f4f34212abe4a4140387", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes"